$description:
Button component tokens.

STRUCTURAL ONLY — on purpose. The variant x colour matrix (4 variants x 8 roles x 4 states) is NOT expressed here. 2.x emitted roughly 350 of those combinations as global custom properties in :root, which is a large part of why the stylesheet is 1.29 MB, and none of them are decisions a designer makes: they are derivations of the role semantics.

Instead the CSS assigns local custom properties per variant/colour selector:

  .df-button[data-variant="solid"][data-color="primary"] {
    --df-button-bg: var(--df-role-primary-base);
    --df-button-fg: var(--df-role-primary-on-base);
  }

A client can still override any single combination with that same selector, and overriding the role instead propagates everywhere at once. What lives here is what a designer genuinely specifies: geometry and type per size.
